" means to find all its roots and prove that there are no other roots.",{"link":222,"schemaName":223,"title":224,"key":225,"seo":226,"description":227},"\u002Farticle\u002Ffoundations\u002Fequations\u002Felementary\u002F?element=same-action-rule","accent_statement","Same Action Rule",{},{},"If the same action is performed on both sides of a true equality, the resulting equality will also be true.",{"link":229,"schemaName":230,"title":231,"key":232,"seo":233,"description":235},"\u002Farticle\u002Ffoundations\u002Fequations\u002Felementary\u002F?element=common-mistakes","list","Mistakes when solving equations",{},{"title":234},"Common mistakes when solving equations","A list of common mistakes that beginners make when solving equations.",{"link":237,"schemaName":238,"title":239,"key":240,"seo":241,"description":242},"\u002Farticle\u002Ffoundations\u002Fequations\u002Felementary\u002F?element=why-solve-equations","heading","Why Solve Equations?",{},{},"A set of examples requiring the ability to solve equations to work with.",{"link":244,"schemaName":238,"title":245,"key":246,"seo":247,"description":249},"\u002Farticle\u002Ffoundations\u002Fequations\u002Felementary\u002F?element=the-idiot-s-triangle","Triangle of Formulas",{},{"title":248},"Magic triangle of formulas","A mnemonic technique for memorizing simple formulas.",{"link":251,"schemaName":238,"title":252,"key":253,"seo":254,"description":256},"\u002Farticle\u002Ffoundations\u002Fequations\u002Felementary\u002F?element=equations-in-life","Equations in Life",{},{"title":255},"Where are equations used in life?","A selection of problems and situations from real life that can be solved if translated into equations.",{"link":258,"schemaName":259,"title":260,"key":261,"seo":262,"description":263},"\u002Fpractice\u002Ffoundations\u002Fequations\u002Felementary\u002F?element=linear-root","problems","Linear equations formula",{},{},"Formula by which you can very quickly find the root of any equation of the form Ax + B = 0.",{"elements":265},{"accent_term":266,"accent_statement":267,"accent_important":268,"problem":269},3,1,4,35,{"type":8,"link":271,"title":272,"description":273,"keyLinks":274,"stats":289},"\u002Fpage\u002Ffoundations\u002Fequations\u002Fzero-product-property\u002F","Zero Product Property","\n    A simple and very effective way to solve equations made of factors (brackets) whose product is zero.\n    You need this method, because a huge number of different equations get reduced to exactly this form.\n  ",[275,281],{"link":276,"schemaName":223,"title":272,"key":277,"seo":278,"description":280},"\u002Fpage\u002Ffoundations\u002Fequations\u002Fzero-product-property\u002F?element=zero-product-method",{},{"title":279},"What is zero product property?","A convenient way to quickly solve equations written as a product of factors equal to zero.",{"link":282,"schemaName":259,"title":283,"key":284,"seo":286,"description":288},"\u002Fpage\u002Ffoundations\u002Fequations\u002Fzero-product-property\u002F?element=zero-product-examples","Practicing zero product property",{"title":285},"Usage examples",{"title":287},"How to use zero product property?","Practice problems for the zero product property with detailed solutions.",{"elements":290},{"accent_statement":267,"problem":267},{"type":184,"link":292,"title":293,"description":294,"stats":295},"\u002Fgroup\u002Ffoundations\u002Fequations\u002Fquadratic\u002F","Quadratic Equations","\n    A comprehensive overview of quadratic equations, including quadratic trinomials, completing the square,\n    the discriminant, Vieta's formulas, factoring, real-life applications, and even methods for solving them mentally.\n  ",{"materials":296,"elements":297},6,{"accent_term":296,"accent_statement":296,"accent_important":298,"problem":299},10,65,{"type":187,"link":301,"title":302},"\u002Farticle\u002Ffoundations\u002Fequations\u002Fequivalence\u002F","Equivalence of equations",{"contributorsCount":267,"sponsorsCount":304},0,{"shortBookId":5,"fron